note long_names_om2: long names in an OM-2 unit: requires and ensures over long parameter names, an
note unsized view with a long name, a part of a long-named local, and a loop invariant over a long name.
note The checks exit 1..3 when they fail; then a requires with left_operand 5000 fails: trap 9, exit 109.
om2
fn bounded_sum left_operand ulong right_operand ulong to ulong
requires lt left_operand 1000
ensures ge result left_operand
ret add left_operand right_operand
end

fn view_length all_the_bytes view uchar * to ulong
ret len all_the_bytes
end

fn main to int
first_total = bounded_sum 5 6
if ne first_total 11
ret 1
end
local_bytes = new uchar 32 7
if ne view_length part local_bytes 4 9 9
ret 2
end
loop_counter = ulong 0
while lt loop_counter 5 bound 10
invariant le loop_counter 5
loop_counter = add loop_counter 1
end
if ne loop_counter 5
ret 3
end
over_limit = bounded_sum 5000 1
ret 4
end
